or node1 failed with an SSH connection reset, so it cannot independently confirm node1's changed boot ID. Executor evidence still shows its old identity, restart acknowledgement, new identity, and recovered configuration and services (global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity; cmd-5ccd68a79b1f4d1d; cmd-c4043f7964f04978; cmd-76fd1f8addc2457c; cmd-1cb3d6d6458f42d9).","The generic failed-service lifecycle observation is unsupported on OpenWrt; node1 health is therefore established through its init-script status, runtime firewall, DHCP/DNS, and client recovery evidence rather than a failed-unit inventory (global:after_executor:node1:failed-services; cmd-520230e704b74677)."]}
